[ceiling] The rear Z-slide heads' square catches stand at Z160.00 + 8.70 + 0.25 running fit + two 0.25 supported-face allowances = 169.45. Both this head underside and the mating back-top foot print down, so the complete 0.75 mm gap is allocated here while the foot remains on its nominal plane. The head retains 5.35 mm of stock up to Z174.8. Its flat bearing resists lift without camming the seam open; the arm returns to the wall on its 45-degree under-flare. The west run is interrupted by the PRV passage, and support is removed through the open slide channels.
