[sliver] The floor recess's 0.25 mm running-clearance returns end beside the handhold inner walls at Y212.8. Each 0.25 by 6 mm face closes a clearance slot and is backed by the continuous floor slab aft of it. The clearance keeps the front floor tongue free of the back piece as their floor and inner-wall scarfs telescope together; the narrow face is not a load-bearing strip.
